(The Lighthouse at Sker Point) Tj
T*
/F1 12 Tf
(by A. Wren \(QA Corpus\)) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(Reader test document - QA fixture) Tj
T*
T*
/F1 13 Tf
(1. The Keeper's Ledger) Tj
T*
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(Maren wrote the log in a hand so small it looked like a line of ants. The wind had been) Tj
T*
(steady for nine days, and the entries repeated themselves: clear at four, clear at eight,) Tj
T*
(nothing on the horizon.) Tj
T*
T*
(She had inherited the ledger with the post. Nobody had explained the job, only the objects -) Tj
T*
(a brass key, a tin of wick, a book with a leather spine and no title. The keeper's rule was) Tj
T*
(simple and unwritten: the light does not go out.) Tj
T*
T*
(On the eleventh day the wind changed direction, and with it came a sound she had never heard) Tj
T*
(before, low and patient, like something large moving slowly under the water of the sound.) Tj
T*
T*
/F1 13 Tf
(2. Fog on the Sound) Tj
T*
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(Fog arrived without ceremony. It simply was there at noon, a soft grey wall that swallowed) Tj
T*
(the harbour and then the last hundred metres of rock below the tower.) Tj
T*
T*
(In fog the work became ritual. Wick trimmed, lens polished, clock wound, log signed. Maren) Tj
T*
(found she liked the ritual. It gave the hours an order the fog had taken away.) Tj
T*
T*
(She talked to the sea a little. It was not madness, exactly; it was the ordinary courtesy of) Tj
T*
(living alone with something that listens. The sea never answered, but it never left either.) Tj
T*
T*
ET
